            <title><![CDATA[Alpine Linux Security advisory: OpenSSH-server password authentication bypass (398 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://alpinelinux.org/posts/2026-11-05-openssh-password-authentication-bypass/</link>
            <guid>50379704</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:44:20 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://alpinelinux.org/posts/2026-11-05-openssh-password-authentication-bypass/">https://alpinelinux.org/posts/2026-11-05-openssh-password-authentication-bypass/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50379704">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div id="content">
                <p><time datetime="2026-11-05">2026-11-05</time>
                </p>
                
<p><strong>If you run <code>sshd</code> on Alpine Linux, update <code>openssh</code> now and restart <code>sshd</code>.</strong>
Upgrading the package alone does not replace the running daemon.</p>
<p>If you cannot update yet, at least disable password logins: set
<code>PasswordAuthentication no</code> in your sshd configuration and restart <code>sshd</code>.
Either one closes the hole.</p>
<h2 id="what-is-the-problem">What is the problem?</h2>
<p>An attacker who can reach your SSH port can log in without knowing any
password. It takes one connection, works every time, and needs no retries.</p>
<p>The attacker needs the name of an account whose password field is <code>*</code>
(an account with no password set, which is normal for key-only accounts), and
needs the machine to have at least one other account with a <code>$5$</code> or <code>$6$</code>
password hash. The attacker then sends a very long password (257 to 1024
bytes). One user with a password is enough: it makes every account without
one reachable.</p>
<p>Details are in the <a href="https://www.openssh.com/releasenotes.html">OpenSSH 10.6p2 release
notes</a>. No CVE identifier had been
assigned at the time of writing.</p>
<h2 id="who-is-affected">Who is affected?</h2>
<p>You are affected if all of the following are true:</p>
<ul>
<li>You run the Alpine <code>openssh-server</code> package, which is built without PAM, or
you run <code>openssh-server-pam</code> with <code>UsePAM no</code>. (<code>openssh-server-pam</code> with
<code>UsePAM yes</code> is not affected.)</li>
<li><code>PasswordAuthentication</code> is <code>yes</code> (the OpenSSH default, unless you changed it).</li>
<li>The machine has an account whose password field is <code>*</code>. This includes:
<ul>
<li><code>root</code>, which ships as <code>root:*</code> in the base image since about Alpine 3.16.
OpenSSH’s default <code>PermitRootLogin prohibit-password</code> protects root, so
root is only reachable if <code>PermitRootLogin yes</code> is set. That does not help if
another account that can log in is able to become root, for example
through <code>doas</code>.</li>
<li>Any key-only user created with <code>adduser</code> without a password, or with
<code>usermod -p '*'</code>.</li>
<li>Users coming from a directory service through musl-nscd (nslcd, winbind,
sssd), since they have no shadow entry.</li>
<li>The <code>alpine</code> user in the official <strong>tiny-cloud</strong> images (see below).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>At least one local account has a <code>$5$</code> or <code>$6$</code> password hash.</li>
</ul>
<p>Affected releases: every Alpine release we checked, 3.21 through 3.24 and
edge, and the older releases that no longer receive regular updates (3.16 to
3.20).</p>
<h3 id="who-is-not-affected">Who is not affected?</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Docker and other container users</strong> that do not run <code>sshd</code> in the
container.</li>
<li>Systems with <code>PasswordAuthentication no</code>.</li>
<li>Systems using <code>openssh-server-pam</code> with <code>UsePAM yes</code> (with <code>UsePAM no</code>
you are affected).</li>
<li>Locked accounts: those with <code>!</code> as the password field in <code>/etc/shadow</code>
(a line starting <code>user:!:</code>). They cannot log in with a password or a key.</li>
<li>Systems where no account has a <code>$</code>-style password hash.</li>
<li>Cloud images configured through cloud-init, which writes
<code>PasswordAuthentication no</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-can-i-fix-it">How can I fix it?</h2>
<h3 id="1-update">1. Update</h3>
<pre><code>apk upgrade -U -a
</code></pre>
<p>Alpine 3.21.10, 3.22.8, 3.23.8 and 3.24.4 contain the fixed package (see the
<a href="https://alpinelinux.org/posts/alpine-3.21.10-3.22.8-3.23.8-3.24.4-released/">release announcement</a>).
The fixed package versions are:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
      <tr>
          <th>Branch</th>
          <th>Fixed <code>openssh</code> version</th>
      </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
      <tr>
          <td>edge</td>
          <td>10.6_p2-r0</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.24</td>
          <td>10.3_p1-r2</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.23</td>
          <td>10.2_p1-r1</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.22</td>
          <td>10.0_p1-r11</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.21</td>
          <td>9.9_p2-r1</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.20</td>
          <td>9.7_p1-r6</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.19</td>
          <td>9.6_p1-r3</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.18</td>
          <td>9.3_p2-r4</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.17</td>
          <td>9.1_p1-r7</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td>3.16</td>
          <td>9.0_p1-r6</td>
      </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Restart <code>sshd</code> after upgrading</strong> (<code>rc-service sshd restart</code>). Upgrading the
package does not restart a running <code>sshd</code>, so you must do it after.</p>
<h3 id="2-if-you-cannot-update-disable-password-authentication">2. If you cannot update: disable password authentication</h3>
<p>Before you start, make sure your SSH key login works, and keep your current
session open until you have tested a new login.</p>
<p>Run these as root. The first two commands create a drop-in file. Alpine’s
default <code>sshd_config</code> reads that directory from 3.19 onward; older releases
ignore it. The <code>sed</code> command changes <code>yes</code> to <code>no</code> on every
<code>PasswordAuthentication</code> line in <code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code>, whatever the spacing,
including lines inside a <code>Match</code> block. It also adds <code>PasswordAuthentication no</code> at the top of the file, for the case where there was no such line, and
saves the original as <code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config.bak</code>. The last two commands check
the configuration, restart the daemon, and show the result:</p>
<pre><code>mkdir -p /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d
echo 'PasswordAuthentication no' &gt; /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-no-passwords.conf
sed -i.bak -e '1i PasswordAuthentication no' \
  -e 's/^\(\s*PasswordAuthentication[^y#]*\)yes/\1no/i' \
  /etc/ssh/sshd_config
sshd -t &amp;&amp; rc-service sshd restart
sshd -T | grep -i passwordauthentication
</code></pre>
<p>The last command should print <code>passwordauthentication no</code>. To undo, delete
<code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-no-passwords.conf</code> and copy
<code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config.bak</code> back over <code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code>.</p>
<h2 id="cloud-images-tiny-cloud">Cloud images (tiny-cloud)</h2>
<p>The official tiny-cloud images (the qcow2, VHD and AMI artifacts) from
<strong>3.18.11 through 3.24.3</strong> ship an <code>alpine</code> user with a <code>*</code> password field and
passwordless <code>doas</code>. They are safe on first boot. They become exploitable as
soon as any <code>$6$</code> hash exists on the machine, for example when an admin sets a
console password, or user-data adds a user with <code>hashed_passwd</code>. An attacker
then gets a shell as <code>alpine</code> and can use <code>doas</code> to become root.</p>
<p>Images built from 3.21.10, 3.22.8, 3.23.8, 3.24.4 and later include the fixed
package. Images from earlier point releases do not, so on every running
instance, update <code>openssh</code> or disable password authentication.</p>
<h2 id="releases-that-are-no-longer-supported-321-and-older">Releases that are no longer supported (3.21 and older)</h2>
<p>These releases have the same bug. 3.21 reached its end of support on
2026-11-01, but we have published fixed packages for each release all the way
back to 3.16.</p>
<h2 id="how-do-i-know-if-i-was-attacked">How do I know if I was attacked?</h2>
<p>Look in <code>/var/log/messages</code> for <code>sshd</code> lines reading <code>Accepted password for</code>
an account that has no password (<code>alpine</code>, <code>root</code>, or any key-only user).
Review <code>doas</code> use and recently created users, files and authorized keys on
exposed machines. If you cannot rule out a login, treat the machine as
compromised.</p>
<h2 id="how-could-this-happen">How could this happen?</h2>
<p>When sshd is built without PAM, it checks a password by hashing the attempt
with <code>crypt()</code> (the C library function that turns a password into its stored
hash) and comparing the result to the stored password field. For an account
whose stored field is too short to contain a salt (the random prefix of a
hash), sshd borrows the salt of another account.</p>
<p>musl’s <code>crypt()</code> returns the string <code>*</code> as an error indicator when the key is
over 256 bytes long. <code>*</code> is also exactly what the stored field contains for
every account with no password, so the “hash” matches and the login succeeds.</p>
<p>OpenSSH 10.6p2 avoids the problem in sshd. The stable-branch packages above
carry a patch for the same problem.</p>
<h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
<p>Reported by Özgün Kültekin of <a href="https://wakefield.co/">Wakefield</a>. Thanks to
Damien Miller and Darren Tucker of the OpenSSH project for the fix and the
10.6p2 release, to Timo Teräs for help analyzing the issue, and to Natanael
Copa, who built and uploaded the updated packages.</p>

            </div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[September in Servo: <progress>, rounded rectangles, and more (126 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://servo.org/blog/2026/11/05/september-in-servo/</link>
            <guid>50379576</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:34:18 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://servo.org/blog/2026/11/05/september-in-servo/">https://servo.org/blog/2026/11/05/september-in-servo/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50379576">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>
  
<p><a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/releases/tag/v0.7.0"><strong>Servo 0.7.0</strong></a> contains all of the changes we landed in September, spanning 527 commits!</p>
<figure>
    <a href="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-gary-banner.png"><img src="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-gary-banner.png" alt="a black and white cat named Gary showing off new visual web platform features"></a>
</figure>
<p>The developer tools console now <strong>eagerly evaluates</strong> JS inputs, allowing faster feedback (<a href="https://github.com/freyacodes">@freyacodes</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47527">#47527</a>).</p>
<p>We’ve shipped new web platform features:</p>
<ul>
<li>the <strong>:checked</strong> pseudoclass (<a href="https://github.com/skyz1">@skyz1</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47987">#47987</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>user-select</strong> property (<a href="https://github.com/SimonSapin">@SimonSapin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48137">#48137</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48242">#48242</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>&lt;progress&gt;</strong> element (<a href="https://github.com/rayguo17">@rayguo17</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/46974">#46974</a>)</li>
<li>CSS <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Values_and_units/Using_typed_arithmetic">typed arithmetic</a> (<a href="https://github.com/Loirooriol">@Loirooriol</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48338">#48338</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>alpha()</strong> CSS function (<a href="https://github.com/Loirooriol">@Loirooriol</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48344">#48344</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>font-width</strong> property (<a href="https://github.com/Loirooriol">@Loirooriol</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47914">#47914</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p>Plus a bunch of new DOM APIs:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>parentRule</strong> on <strong>CSSRule</strong> and <strong>CSSStyleDeclaration</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/skyz1">@skyz1</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47743">#47743</a>)</li>
<li><strong>version</strong> on <strong>HTMLHtmlElement</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/SilvioPilato">@SilvioPilato</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47786">#47786</a>)</li>
<li><strong>getComposedRanges()</strong> and <strong>direction</strong> on <strong>Selection</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47683">#47683</a>)</li>
<li><strong>baseURL</strong> on <strong>CSSStyleSheet</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Gae24">@Gae24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47783">#47783</a>)</li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Modules#loading_non-javascript_resources"><strong>CSS modules</strong></a>(<a href="https://github.com/Gae24">@Gae24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47813">#47813</a>) and <strong>text modules</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Gae24">@Gae24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47863">#47863</a>)</li>
<li><strong>getContextAttributes()</strong> on <strong>CanvasRenderingContext2D</strong> and <strong>OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Taym95">@Taym95</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47868">#47868</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>Content-Language</strong> header (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47930">#47930</a>)</li>
<li><strong>dir</strong> on <strong>Document</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48170">#48170</a>)</li>
<li><strong>SVGAElement</strong>, <strong>SVGPatternElement</strong>, <strong>SVGTSpanElement</strong>, <strong>SVGTextContentElement</strong>, <strong>SVGTextElement</strong>, <strong>SVGTextPositioningElement</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mu-mostafa98">@mu-mostafa98</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48174">#48174</a>)</li>
<li>the <strong>MLKEM768-X25519</strong> algorithm for <strong>WebCrypto</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/kkoyung">@kkoyung</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48240">#48240</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48282">#48282</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48313">#48313</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48350">#48350</a>)</li>
<li><strong>roundRect()</strong> on <strong>CanvasRenderingContext2D</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48293">#48293</a>)</li>
<li><strong>paintTime</strong> and <strong>presentationTime</strong> on <strong>PerformancePaintTiming</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/shubhamg13">@shubhamg13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47926">#47926</a>)</li>
<li><strong>getCueAsHTML()</strong> on <strong>VTTCue</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48146">#48146</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="security" tabindex="-1">Security <a href="#security">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>We upgraded to <strong>SpiderMonkey v153.3</strong> and <strong>mozangle v0.7</strong>, both of which included fixes for security bugs reported upstream (<a href="https://github.com/sagudev">@sagudev</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48176">#48176</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47655">#47655</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48259">#48259</a>).</p>
<h2 id="real-world-compat" tabindex="-1">Real world compat <a href="#real-world-compat">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>The <a href="https://www.egui.rs/">egui.rs</a> demo now works as expected with <code>--pref dom._webegpu_enabled</code>.</p>
<figure>
    <a href="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-egui.png"><img src="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-egui.png" alt="http://egui.rs rendering in Servo"></a>
</figure>
<p>This <a href="https://jooyouss.github.io/candy-crush/">Candy Crush</a> game is now playable.</p>
<figure>
    <a href="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-candycrush.png"><img src="https://servo.org/img/blog/2026-10-candycrush.png" alt="A Candy Crush game rendering in Servo"></a>
</figure>
<p>We’re interested to hear how well your favourite websites run in Servo! Report successes in <a href="https://servo.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/263398-general/topic/Servo.20web.20compat.20success.20stories/with/612898341">this Zulip thread</a> or <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/discussions/49037">this Github discussion</a>, and failures <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/issues">in our GitHub issues</a>.</p>
<h2 id="work-in-progress" tabindex="-1">Work in progress <a href="#work-in-progress">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>Our accessibility tree (<code>--pref accessibility_enabled</code>) now <strong>reports geometry bounds</strong> for inline elements (<a href="https://github.com/alice">@alice</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47905">#47905</a>) and does much less work when responding to DOM changes (<a href="https://github.com/alice">@alice</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47690">#47690</a>).
Additionally, elements with <code>display: none</code> are reported as hidden (<a href="https://github.com/alice">@alice</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47772">#47772</a>).</p>
<p>We had lots of conformance improvements for our <strong>WebGL2 implementation</strong> (<code>--pref dom_webgl2_enabled</code>) (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48423">#48423</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48441">#48441</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48470">#48470</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48479">#48479</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48495">#48495</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48473">#48473</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48536">#48536</a>).</p>
<p>Support for WSIWYG editors (which rely heavily on <strong><code>contenteditable</code></strong>) is going very well: keyboard inputs are now hooked up when <code>--pref dom_exec_command_enabled</code> is present, so many editors are now usable (<a href="https://www.tiny.cloud/docs/tinymce/latest/basic-example/">example</a>).</p>
<p><strong>Closed captioning</strong> for video elements is making progress.
Text tracks now fire <code>enter</code>, <code>exit</code>, and <code>cuechange</code> events (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47725">#47725</a>).
Media elements now return the full sorted list of text tracks (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47785">#47785</a>), and adding cues to a text track now sets that track correctly (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48012">#48012</a>).
Text track objects now reflect the attributes of the associated <code>&lt;track&gt;</code> element.
Text track URLs are fetched at the correct time (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48325">#48325</a>), and active cues are computed correctly (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48305">#48305</a>), while text track cues are ordered as expected (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48368">#48368</a>).
Additionally, WebVTT parsing can now recover from errors (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48391">#48391</a>).</p>
<p>The <strong>Sanitizer API</strong> (<code>--pref dom_sanitizer_enabled</code>) now accepts the <code>javascriptURLs</code> property (<a href="https://github.com/skyz1">@skyz1</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47867">#47867</a>).</p>
<p><strong>IndexedDB</strong> continues to improve: tables no longer error if unrelated tables contain duplicate index names (<code>--pref dom_indexeddb_enabled</code>) (<a href="https://github.com/leowatts">@leowatts</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47936">#47936</a>).
Additionally, we implemented <strong>openCursor()</strong> and <strong>openKeyCursor()</strong> on <strong>IDBIndex</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/kuntal-devrat">@kuntal-devrat</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48281">#48281</a>), as well as <strong>advance()</strong>, <strong>continue()</strong>, and <strong>continuePrimaryKey()</strong> on <strong>IDBCursor</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/kuntal-devrat">@kuntal-devrat</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48400">#48400</a>).</p>
<p>We implemented the <strong>getTimeline()</strong> and <strong>setTimeline()</strong> methods for the <strong>Animation</strong> interface (<code>--pref dom_web_animations_enabled</code>) (<a href="https://github.com/simonwuelker">@simonwuelker</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48122">#48122</a>).</p>
<h2 id="embedding-api" tabindex="-1">Embedding API <a href="#embedding-api">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>There’s a new API for events originating from accessibility tools: <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.Servo.html"><code>Servo</code></a>::<a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.Servo.html#method.forward_accessibility_action"><code>forward_accessibility_action</code></a> (<a href="https://github.com/alice">@alice</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48512">#48512</a>).</p>
<p>There is also an API to clear session history: <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html"><code>WebView</code></a>::<a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html#method.clear_session_history"><code>clear_session_history</code></a> (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47483">#47483</a>).</p>
<p>The <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html"><code>WebView</code></a>::<code>set_throttled</code> API has been removed (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/39923">#39923</a>).
Throttling automatically occurs when a WebView is <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html#method.hide">hidden</a> and is stopped when <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html#method.show">shown</a>.</p>
<p>The <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/trait.WebViewDelegate.html"><code>WebViewDelegate</code></a>::<code>notify_focus_changed</code> method was removed, along with the <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.Servo.html"><code>Servo</code></a> methods <code>focus</code> and <code>blur</code> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48364">#48364</a>).
Embedders must call <a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html"><code>WebView</code></a>::<a href="https://doc.servo.org/servo/struct.WebView.html#method.set_focused"><code>set_focused</code></a> whenever a WebView has gained or lost system focus.</p>
<p>The <code>webgl</code> feature has been added to the <code>default_web_features</code> feature (<a href="https://github.com/janeoa">@janeoa</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47866">#47866</a>).
If an embedding does not want to ship with WebGL support they will now need to disable default features.</p>
<p>Multiprocess mode is enabled at build time with the new Cargo feature <code>multprocess</code> (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47360">#47360</a>).
To remove support for this feature (reducing binary size by ~2MB), build Servo with default features disabled.</p>
<p>Two new preferences exist to tune garbage collector behaviour: <code>js_mem_gc_malloc_threshold_base_mb</code> and <code>js_mem_gc_urgent_threshold_mb</code> (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47999">#47999</a>).
These can help on memory-constrained devices, and more information is available in the SpiderMonkey source (<a href="https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/28b7a7bffb5f82828143d9ad63839ad263b598be/js/src/gc/Scheduling.h#425-429">base</a>, <a href="https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/28b7a7bffb5f82828143d9ad63839ad263b598be/js/src/gc/Scheduling.h#440-445">urgent</a>).</p>
<p>The JVM compatibility target was raised to 11 on Android (<a href="https://github.com/veyndan">@veyndan</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48414">#48414</a>).</p>
<h2 id="for-users-and-developers" tabindex="-1">For users and developers <a href="#for-users-and-developers">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>It is now possible to cross-compile the OpenHarmony build from Windows hosts (<a href="https://github.com/jschwe">@jschwe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48392">#48392</a>).</p>
<p>Unhandled promise rejections are reported to the JS console (<a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48486">#48486</a>), making it easier to narrow down web compatibility issues in Servo.</p>
<p>The OpenHarmony SDK was updated to API level 23 (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48505">#48505</a>).</p>
<p>Pressing Control+A (or Command+A on macOS) now selects all the content in a document (<a href="https://github.com/dzfrias">@dzfrias</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48025">#48025</a>).
It is no longer possible to copy text inside of password inputs (<a href="https://github.com/dzfrias">@dzfrias</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48404">#48404</a>).</p>
<p>Embedder-originating JS (e.g. devtools console or embedding APIs) will always execute, even in documents that disable scripting via sandboxing or CSP (<a href="https://github.com/derdilla">@derdilla</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48394">#48394</a>).</p>
<h2 id="performance-and-stability" tabindex="-1">Performance and stability <a href="#performance-and-stability">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>We improved performance by removing <strong>unnecessary allocations</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47689">#47689</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47839">#47839</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47838">#47838</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47982">#47982</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48006">#48006</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48036">#48036</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48099">#48099</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48204">#48204</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48127">#48127</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48218">#48218</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48357">#48357</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48386">#48386</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48422">#48422</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48440">#48440</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48452">#48452</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48508">#48508</a>), <strong>preallocating more</strong> when building vectors (<a href="https://github.com/jschwe">@jschwe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/sagudev">@sagudev</a>, <a href="https://github.com/webbeef">@webbeef</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47455">#47455</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47613">#47613</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48026">#48026</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48398">#48398</a>), and <strong>avoiding IPC</strong> in single process mode (<a href="https://github.com/leowatts">@leowatts</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Uiniel">@Uiniel</a>, <a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47691">#47691</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47718">#47718</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48002">#48002</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48073">#48073</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48476">#48476</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48435">#48435</a>).</p>
<p>We also sped up Servo by reducing interactions with the GC (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47818">#47818</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48257">#48257</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48396">#48396</a>), and doing less work when modifying selections (<a href="https://github.com/SimonSapin">@SimonSapin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47579">#47579</a>), dispatching events (<a href="https://github.com/webbeef">@webbeef</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48078">#48078</a>), calculating font metrics (<a href="https://github.com/RichardTjokroutomo">@RichardTjokroutomo</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48238">#48238</a>), and indexing window frames (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47832">#47832</a>).</p>
<p>We <strong>reduced memory usage</strong> in common cases by reusing buffers (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47751">#47751</a>), clearing more page-specific data (<a href="https://github.com/Radeonares32">@Radeonares32</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/jschwe">@jschwe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47651">#47651</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47806">#47806</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47805">#47805</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48166">#48166</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48295">#48295</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48297">#48297</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48016">#48016</a>), compacting data structures (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/webbeef">@webbeef</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SimonSapin">@SimonSapin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47776">#47776</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48039">#48039</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48050">#48050</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47742">#47742</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48301">#48301</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48296">#48296</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48105">#48105</a>), and sharing more buffers (<a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47998">#47998</a>).
We also fixed a memory leak involving <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> elements (<a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48371">#48371</a>).</p>
<p>We turned on <strong>thread affinity boosting</strong> on Linux, which can improve performance on some CPU architectures (<a href="https://github.com/jschwe">@jschwe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47058">#47058</a>).</p>
<p>We’re working on statically preventing <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/issues/39139">a footgun</a> that can lead to uncollectible GC cycles and leaking memory (<a href="https://github.com/Gae24">@Gae24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/lumiscosity">@lumiscosity</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SilvioPilato">@SilvioPilato</a>, <a href="https://github.com/sahilnyk">@sahilnyk</a>, <a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/kuntal-devrat">@kuntal-devrat</a>, <a href="https://github.com/MohamedAli00949">@MohamedAli00949</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47941">#47941</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48013">#48013</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48021">#48021</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48035">#48035</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48033">#48033</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48051">#48051</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48072">#48072</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48171">#48171</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48209">#48209</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48248">#48248</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48246">#48246</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48264">#48264</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48285">#48285</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48311">#48311</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48408">#48408</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48053">#48053</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48156">#48156</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48186">#48186</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48223">#48223</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48315">#48315</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47872">#47872</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47698">#47698</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47682">#47682</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47735">#47735</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47816">#47816</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47817">#47817</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47794">#47794</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47909">#47909</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47934">#47934</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47935">#47935</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47954">#47954</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48022">#48022</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47955">#47955</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48058">#48058</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48228">#48228</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48247">#48247</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48261">#48261</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48280">#48280</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48302">#48302</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48316">#48316</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48328">#48328</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48346">#48346</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48355">#48355</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48262">#48262</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48377">#48377</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48304">#48304</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48378">#48378</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48388">#48388</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48432">#48432</a>).</p>
<p>We fixed panics in <strong>WebRTC</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/MunishMummadi">@MunishMummadi</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/4772">#4772</a>), <strong>execCommand()</strong> on <strong>Document</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47784">#47784</a>), <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> (<a href="https://github.com/calvaris">@calvaris</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/46148">#46148</a>), <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code> (<a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48465">#48465</a>), <strong>SharedWorker</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47940">#47940</a>), <strong>ancestorOrigins</strong> on <strong>Document</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48009">#48009</a>), <code>about:memory</code> (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47686">#47686</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48001">#48001</a>), and EGL 1.4 configurations (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47803">#47803</a>).</p>
<p>We also fixed a very ironic panic triggered by the <code>about:crash</code> page that loads when a normal page triggers a panic (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48055">#48055</a>)</p>
<p>The JS console no longer hangs when primitive values as thrown as exceptions (<a href="https://github.com/FatCat560">@FatCat560</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47629">#47629</a>).
Servo no longer hangs on shutdown in multiprocess mode (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48523">#48523</a>), when certain pages use <strong>IntersectionObserver</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47693">#47693</a>), when closing a browsing context with pending WebDriver commands (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48131">#48131</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48172">#48172</a>), or when closing <strong>SharedWorker</strong>s (<a href="https://github.com/nicoburns">@nicoburns</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48477">#48477</a>).</p>
<p><code>about:memory</code> got more improvements: we measure more memory for SVG rendering (<a href="https://github.com/Narfinger">@Narfinger</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47061">#47061</a>), WebAudio (<a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47996">#47996</a>), and identify globals that have been leaked (<a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48237">#48237</a>).</p>
<h2 id="more-on-the-web-platform" tabindex="-1">More on the web platform <a href="#more-on-the-web-platform">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>CSS images now <strong>delay the <code>load</code> event</strong>, leading to more consistent behaviour for engine users performing visual rendering (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48199">#48199</a>).</p>
<p>Interactive selections in documents continued to improve!
They now can span shadow trees (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SimonSapin">@SimonSapin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47931">#47931</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47694">#47694</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47895">#47895</a>), and have consistent heights and positions (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47937">#47937</a>), plus there are new context menu entries to copy and select all (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48101">#48101</a>).
Additionally, image-based content shows when it is part of a selection (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48149">#48149</a>).</p>
<p><code>Window.open()</code> respects sandbox flags that prevent popups (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47653">#47653</a>).</p>
<p><strong>LargestContentfulPaint</strong> now reports the <strong>loadTime</strong> for image content (<a href="https://github.com/shubhamg13">@shubhamg13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48286">#48286</a>), ignores cross-origin frames (<a href="https://github.com/shubhamg13">@shubhamg13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48094">#48094</a>), ignores invisible text (<a href="https://github.com/shubhamg13">@shubhamg13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48010">#48010</a>), and reports null elements when they are removed from the tree (<a href="https://github.com/shubhamg13">@shubhamg13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48125">#48125</a>).</p>
<p><strong>select()</strong> on a text input now focuses the control (<a href="https://github.com/dzfrias">@dzfrias</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48475">#48475</a>).</p>
<p>Our WebDriver server now automates setting permissions (<a href="https://github.com/xbwwj">@xbwwj</a>, <a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47623">#47623</a>), while sending click events and keyboard actions uses fewer delays (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48066">#48066</a>).</p>
<p>There are more useful error messages for methods on <strong>Document</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/eachra-bawn">@eachra-bawn</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47835">#47835</a>) and <strong>CSS</strong>-related interfaces (<a href="https://github.com/eachra-bawn">@eachra-bawn</a>, <a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47746">#47746</a>).</p>
<p>We upgraded our <a href="https://crates.io/crates/stylo">stylo</a> dependency, which improves compatibility with <strong>contrast-color()</strong>, <strong>color-mix()</strong>, <strong>vertical-align</strong>, <strong>list-style</strong>, <strong>place-items</strong>, <strong>at-rule()</strong>, <strong>calc()</strong>, <strong>alpha()</strong>, <strong>attr()</strong>, <strong>content: attr()</strong>, and <strong>named-feature()</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Loirooriol">@Loirooriol</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/46987">#46987</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47942">#47942</a>).</p>
<p>We also fixed bugs related to <strong>visibilityState</strong> on <strong>Document</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47908">#47908</a>), <strong>containsNode()</strong> on <strong>Selection</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47938">#47938</a>), <strong>setKeyframes</strong> on <strong>KeyframeEffect</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/simonwuelker">@simonwuelker</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48103">#48103</a>), selections when focusing a text input (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48107">#48107</a>), <strong>AudioParam</strong> clamping and automation (<a href="https://github.com/kevlu93">@kevlu93</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48351">#48351</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48347">#48347</a>), <strong>PannerNode</strong> outputs (<a href="https://github.com/kevlu93">@kevlu93</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48510">#48510</a>), the <strong>muted</strong> attribute on <strong>HTMLMediaElement</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48403">#48403</a>), placeholders in text inputs (<a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47761">#47761</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47797">#47797</a>), animations when modifying document stylesheets (<a href="https://github.com/SharanRP">@SharanRP</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48000">#48000</a>), gradient color stops (<a href="https://github.com/BudiArb">@BudiArb</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48288">#48288</a>), sticky table rows (<a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48380">#48380</a>), <strong>::first-letter</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/Loirooriol">@Loirooriol</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48307">#48307</a>), <strong>text-wrap-mode</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48469">#48469</a>), OTF fonts (<a href="https://github.com/wood-ghost">@wood-ghost</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47904">#47904</a>), CSS and nosniff (<a href="https://github.com/sahvx655-wq">@sahvx655-wq</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/45481">#45481</a>), <strong>Sec-Fetch-</strong> headers and redirects (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48203">#48203</a>), <strong>moveBefore()</strong> on <strong>Node</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47692">#47692</a>), <strong>supports()</strong> on <strong>WebCrypto</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/kkoyung">@kkoyung</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47768">#47768</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47891">#47891</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47953">#47953</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47984">#47984</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48410">#48410</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47545">#47545</a>), cross-origin windows (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/jdm">@jdm</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47632">#47632</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48411">#48411</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48038">#48038</a>), origins of <code>about:blank</code> and <code>about:srcdoc</code> (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47630">#47630</a>), <code>keypress</code> events (<a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48324">#48324</a>), text and media documents (<a href="https://github.com/SilvioPilato">@SilvioPilato</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47823">#47823</a>), <strong>body()</strong> on <strong>Response</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48409">#48409</a>), <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> (<a href="https://github.com/TimvdLippe">@TimvdLippe</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48224">#48224</a>), editing hidden inputs (<a href="https://github.com/dzfrias">@dzfrias</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48165">#48165</a>), attribute nodes in XPath (<a href="https://github.com/leowatts">@leowatts</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrobinson">@mrobinson</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47912">#47912</a>), absolutely positioned boxes (<a href="https://github.com/mxmgorin">@mxmgorin</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48081">#48081</a>), CSS Grid containers with absolutely positioned nodes (<a href="https://github.com/nicoburns">@nicoburns</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47519">#47519</a>), <strong>WebDriver</strong> wheel/pointer actions (<a href="https://github.com/yezhizhen">@yezhizhen</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48143">#48143</a>), and <strong>blob:</strong> URLs (<a href="https://github.com/Gae24">@Gae24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47910">#47910</a>).</p>
<h2 id="new-contributors" tabindex="-1">New contributors <a href="#new-contributors">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>A special thanks to the following people for landing their first patch in Servo:</p>
<ul>
<li>Arnau Camprubí (<a href="https://github.com/Arnau478">@Arnau478</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47726">#47726</a>)</li>
<li>Silvio Pilato (<a href="https://github.com/SilvioPilato">@SilvioPilato</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47786">#47786</a>)</li>
<li>Radeonares32 (<a href="https://github.com/Radeonares32">@Radeonares32</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47651">#47651</a>)</li>
<li>derdilla (<a href="https://github.com/derdilla">@derdilla</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47828">#47828</a>)</li>
<li>pr3pony (<a href="https://github.com/pr3pony">@pr3pony</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48030">#48030</a>)</li>
<li>Mario (<a href="https://github.com/Fatcat560">@Fatcat560</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/47629">#47629</a>)</li>
<li>TtyChud (<a href="https://github.com/TTyChud">@TTyChud</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48228">#48228</a>)</li>
<li>Devrate Kuntal (<a href="https://github.com/kuntal-devrat">@kuntal-devrat</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48247">#48247</a>)</li>
<li>Diego Frias (<a href="https://github.com/dzfrias">@dzfrias</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48025">#48025</a>)</li>
<li>LiamillionSS (<a href="https://github.com/LiamillionSS">@LiamillionSS</a>, <a href="https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/48424">#48424</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p>Interested in helping build a web browser?
Take a look at our <a href="https://starters.servo.org/">curated list</a> of issues that are good for new contributors!</p>
<h2 id="donations" tabindex="-1">Donations <a href="#donations">
        <span><i></i></span>
      </a></h2>
<p>Thanks again for your generous support!
We are now receiving <strong>8144 USD/month</strong> (+1% from August) in recurring donations.
This helps us cover the cost of our <strong><a href="https://ci0.servo.org/">speedy</a> <a href="https://ci1.servo.org/">CI</a> <a href="https://ci2.servo.org/">and</a> <a href="https://ci3.servo.org/">benchmarking</a> <a href="https://ci4.servo.org/">servers</a></strong>, one of our latest <strong><a href="https://www.outreachy.org/alums/2026-05/#:~:text=Servo">Outreachy interns</a></strong>, and funding <strong><a href="https://servo.org/blog/2026/09/15/one-year-of-sponsorship/">maintainer work</a></strong> that helps more people contribute to Servo.</p>
<p>Servo is also on <a href="https://thanks.dev/">thanks.dev</a>, and already <strong>37 GitHub users</strong> (+1 from August) that depend on Servo are sponsoring us there.
If you use Servo libraries like <a href="https://crates.io/crates/url/reverse_dependencies">url</a>, <a href="https://crates.io/crates/html5ever/reverse_dependencies">html5ever</a>, <a href="https://crates.io/crates/selectors/reverse_dependencies">selectors</a>, or <a href="https://crates.io/crates/cssparser/reverse_dependencies">cssparser</a>, signing up for <a href="https://thanks.dev/">thanks.dev</a> could be a good way for you (or your employer) to give back to the community.</p>
<p>We now have <a href="https://servo.org/blog/2025/11/21/sponsorship-tiers/"><strong>sponsorship tiers</strong></a> that allow you or your organisation to donate to the Servo project with public acknowlegement of your support.
If you’re interested in this kind of sponsorship, please contact us at <a href="https://servo.org/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#ff95909691bf8c9a8d8990d1908d98"><span data-cfemail="a4cecbcdcae4d7c1d6d2cb8acbd6c3">[email&nbsp;protected]</span></a>.</p>
<figure><div>
        <p><strong>8128</strong> USD/month</p>
        
        
        <p><strong>10000</strong></p>
    </div></figure>
<p>Use of donations is decided transparently via the Technical Steering Committee’s public <strong><a href="https://github.com/servo/project/blob/main/FUNDING_REQUEST.md">funding request process</a></strong>, and active proposals are tracked in <a href="https://github.com/servo/project/issues/187">servo/project#187</a>.
For more details, head to our <a href="https://servo.org/sponsorship/">Sponsorship page</a>.</p>



  
