            <title><![CDATA[MCP Explained (172 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://mcp-explained.com/</link>
            <guid>50379249</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:08:35 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://mcp-explained.com/">https://mcp-explained.com/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50379249">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>
  <div id="intro" aria-label="What is MCP?">
      <p>Model Context Protocol</p>
      <h2>What is MCP?</h2>
      <p>An open standard for connecting AI apps to the tools and data they use. A server says what it can do, the app shows that to the model, and when the model wants something the app calls the server and hands the result back.</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>Host</dt><dd>the AI app you use: Claude, Cursor, ChatGPT, an agent</dd>
        <dt>Server</dt><dd>a small program exposing tools, data or prompts</dd>
        <dt>Model</dt><dd>decides what to use; never talks to a server directly</dd>
        <dt>Not REST</dt><dd>JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout or one HTTP endpoint, and servers can talk back</dd>
        <dt>Not just JSON-RPC</dt><dd>JSON-RPC is the envelope. MCP defines what goes in it: the methods, capability negotiation, transports and auth</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>or jump to <a href="#tools">Tools</a> · <a href="#transports@2024-11-05">the spec time machine</a> · <a href="#poisoning">Break it</a></p>
    </div>
  <div id="left" aria-label="Lessons"><h2>Model Context Protocol</h2></div>
  <div id="center">
        <h2>Message flow <span id="flowcount"></span></h2>
        
      </div>
  
</div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
