  <p><img alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' fill='%2348a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Reading</h2>
  <div>
    <p>Columns of text reflow a lot when the window changes size, so this is a good place to try a resize launch. Each line of text is its own floor. Walkers can drop from line to line, fall off the end of a short line, and land on whatever is below.</p>
    <p>Lines sit closer together than a walker is tall, so text never blocks them. Only borders, boxes, buttons, images and fields do. That keeps walkers from getting stuck between two lines of a paragraph.</p>
    <p>Near the bottom of the page there is one long floor to catch anything that falls all the way down.</p>
  </div>
